<http://digistrucmed.org/text-unit/lu_66f14f762d9ed93be7e45532f52e341584cfa69a96a4b48ae6ab5277a1a358e7_n0076/tu_0003> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Percutaneous edge-to-edge mitral valve repair should be considered in carefully selected patients with secondary mitral regurgitation, not eligible for surgery and not needing coronary revascularization, who are symptomatic c despite OMT and who fulfil criteria d for achieving a reduction in HF hospitalizations. 612" .
